    "citations": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00132",
        "explanation": "Doctor gave a concrete near-term follow-up and materials plan.",
        "quote": "3天后去产科门诊复查时，请带上"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00147",
        "explanation": "Patient demonstrated receipt of escalation triggers and the follow-up plan.",
        "quote": "就不等门诊直接急诊"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00147",
        "explanation": "Patient confirmed she had organized materials for the responsible clinic.",
        "quote": "3天后带去产科看"
      }
    ],
    "executable": true,
    "explanation": "By the end, the patient had a practical plan to continue observed medication administration, attend a 3-day obstetric visit, bring the old ultrasound, discharge drug list, and medication boxes, and seek emergency care for worsening bleeding, pain, fever, dizziness, or watery discharge. Closure is traceable and largely safe at the endpoint, though earlier medication-chain handling and fetal-movement messaging were not erased.",
